<title>USA: TI to sell mobile computer unit to Acer.</title>
<headline>TI to sell mobile computer unit to Acer.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas Instruments Inc said Thursday it had reached a definitive agreement to sell its mobile computing business to Taiwan-based Acer Inc.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Products covered by the sale include TI's TravelMate and Extensa computer lines and associated assets.</p>
<p>TI said its calculator business is not included in the sale agreement.</p>
<p>TI said it expects a substantial number of its mobile computing business employees will transfer to Acer.</p>
<p>It said it expects to close the sale, which is subject to government approvals, on or before March 31.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
